Done. Committed `5aacac1`.

**What I changed:** `src/rtk.rs` — `is_simple_command()` now respects backslash-escaped shell metacharacters. Previously `echo foo \| bar` (where `\|` is a literal pipe argument, not an operator) was misclassified as a complex command, so RTK output compression was skipped even though the command was safe to prefix. The fix mirrors the existing escape handling used for quotes, and treats escaped `|`, `;`, `&`, `>`, `<` as literals while still catching real operators after them.

**Verification:** Wrote the regression test first (confirmed it failed), then the fix. Full gate passes: `cargo fmt` ✅, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` ✅, `cargo build` ✅, `cargo test` ✅ (88 passed, 0 failed). One file changed, no doc updates needed — internal RTK-detection detail, not user-facing behavior.
